    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d256-a2">

                <pb facs="0233" n="159" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg159"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Gibbons to X. Y.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">New York,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-10"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 10, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>“Your note of the 8th instant received, and, in answer, would say that it is my
                    intention of raising at least 3,000 men out of this county to co-operate with a
                    larger body, either to invade Mexico or British America. If we can gain the
                    consent of the President of the United States to this enterprise we will do so.
                    If not, we will go anyhow.</p>
                <p>“Respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>“GEO. W. GIBBONS,</signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>“<hi rendition="#italic">Box</hi> 44, <hi rendition="#italic">Brooklyn
                            Post Office.”</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Note.—</hi>The reply is enclosed in an envelope
                        with the stamp of R. H Gibbons.&amp; Co., real estate agency, 446 Broome
                        street, New York, and postmarked New York.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
